{
  "id": "build/new/bad-id-and-tier",
  "title": "build new rejects an id that is not kebab-case, an unknown tier and bad arguments before touching the file system",
  "source": [
    "intended: docs/decisions.md D7 and the templates row of the other decisions (a new build starts as a draft from a template: invalid until every empty value is filled)"
  ],
  "status": {
    "ts": "xfail",
    "go": "pass"
  },
  "defect": "N-14",
  "intent": "INTENDED behavior (defect N-14, shipped core and templates; docs/decisions.md D7). The id is the launcher's pattern (a lower-case letter, then lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, at most 64 characters): anything else is `JITSO REJECTED: build id must be kebab-case`. The tier is `worker`, `conductor` or `subagent`: anything else is `JITSO REJECTED: --tier must be worker, conductor or subagent`. No id is `JITSO REJECTED: build new needs a build id`, `--tier` with no value is `JITSO REJECTED: --tier needs a value`, any other word or flag is an unknown argument. All exit 2, are checked before the project is read, and leave no folder behind. The oracle has no `build new` (the runner maps only `build list`): it answers `unknown command` on stderr with exit 2, so every expectation that needs the written file or the printed line FAILS on it.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "run": [
        "build",
        "new",
        "Bad_ID"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": [
          {
            "empty": true
          }
        ],
        "stderr": [
          {
            "equals": "JITSO REJECTED: build id must be kebab-case\n"
          }
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": ".jitso/drafts",
            "exists": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "build",
        "new",
        "../x"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": [
          {
            "empty": true
          }
        ],
        "stderr": [
          {
            "equals": "JITSO REJECTED: build id must be kebab-case\n"
          }
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": ".jitso/drafts",
            "exists": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "build",
        "new",
        "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": [
